<title>USA: Hybridon says gets FDA clearance for study.</title>
<headline>Hybridon says gets FDA clearance for study.</headline>
<dateline>WORCESTER, Mass. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hybridon Inc said the U.S. Food and Drug Administration cleared its investigational new drug (IND) application for GEM 132, which the company plans to test as a treatment for cytomegalovirus retinitis.</p>
<p>The company said it will begin enrolling patients in a Phase I/II clinical trial of GEM 132.</p>
<p>Cytomegalovirus retinitis is an infection that can cause blindness in late stage AIDS patients.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
